Notebook[{
Cell["CubeMomentHigherGrades", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"041db5cd-6557-4a37-836e-eb34e84595af"],

Cell["THE MOMENTS BEYOND THE SIX:", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"a5daa840-2949-442f-9882-a23a4133af61"],

Cell["WHICH ARE NEEDED, AND DOES THE ENGINE REACH THEM?", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d42012fc-4ba6-4a30-870a-1b248c362614"],

Cell["\<\
The hierarchy of degree q (displacement expanded to q-th gradients about the \
centre, the equation and its first q derivatives imposed at the centre) needs \
the moments of grade (D, W) = (derivatives on G, degree of the weight)\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f8579b8e-d1de-4de7-8dc6-c0da4b81fc6e"],

Cell["\<\
       density term   :  D = m,      W <= q,      m = 0..q,   D + W even
       stiffness term :  D = m + 1,  W <= q - 1,  m = 0..q,   D + W even.\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"271e0af2-a32e-4649-89a1-c375876b6401"],

Cell["\<\
q = 2 gives the six of the Basic System, G (0,0), K (0,2), N (1,1), M (2,0), \
P (2,2), Q (3,1).  On the layer the order of convergence with both contrasts \
is 2 for q = 1, 2;  4 for q = 3, 4;  6 for q = 5, 6 \
(ContinuumLimit_GradientHierarchy.wl, 36/36).  So:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"587f2ed2-7ac5-49c1-9ab8-22c9d51ce6ae"],

Cell["\<\
fourth order needs q = 3:  four new grades  (1,3) (3,3) (4,0) (4,2) sixth  \
order needs q = 5:  fifteen new grades in all (listed by [1]).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"033765d4-82e3-47a4-8342-82c963b0030c"],

Cell["\<\
Each moment reduces to the scalar moments  E[m; d1..dD'; w1..wW]  of r^m, \
with D' = D or D + 2 (the tensor's own d_i d_n), which CubeMomentCore.wl \
evaluates for any D' and W by peeling derivatives onto the faces.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35e328b7-273d-40e7-9048-bc2685cf06e5"],

Cell["\<\
THE GATES.  A new grade is trusted only if it passes checks with answers \
known independently of the engine:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e13dd8e9-d051-4150-b737-7e4dd4569697"],

Cell["\<\
     (a) the Laplacian chain   Sum_p E[m; {p,p} + rest; w] = m (m+1) E[m-2; \
rest; w]   for m >= 1,
         because Lap r^m = m (m+1) r^(m-2);
     (b) the delta rule        Sum_p E[-1; {p,p} + rest; w] = -4 Pi \
(-1)^|rest| (d_rest w)(0),
         because Lap (1/r) = -4 Pi delta: the sharp test that the \
distributional
         content (the Eshelby delta and its derivatives) is present and \
right;
     (c) parity: E vanishes unless every axis carries an even number of \
indices.\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"4fa00399-d087-4048-8898-ef909d3f6f54"],

Cell["\<\
This file: [1] lists the grades;  [2] runs (a), (b), (c) on the new grades of \
q = 3 and times them;  [3] the same for q = 5, as far as the time allows.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b7753ff1-6b28-4ae9-bd7e-a67cd6e46df2"],

Cell["\<\
Run:  wolframscript -file Mathematica/CubeMomentHigherGrades.wl [maxGradeSum]\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"99772df3-9c9d-4a31-a526-e295a640dc2d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

